SUMMARY:National Disability Employment Awareness Month 2026
DESCRIPTION:Since the 1970s\, National Disability Employment Awareness Month (NDEAM) has taken place every October. NDEAM reinforces the message across the U.S. that people with disabilities provide invaluable roles and perspectives to our diverse American workforce. \nThe Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) reports that one in four adults (at least 60 million) in the U.S. live with a disability. This statistic is based on what is reported\, however. So\, it’s possible that the number is higher than what is stated.
URL:https://hatefreetogether.org/event/national-disability-employment-awareness-month-2026/
CATEGORIES:Season of Connection
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://hatefreetogether.org/wp-content/uploads/National-Disability-Employment-Awareness-v2.webp
END:VEVENT
